{'symbol': 'LUMN', 'date': '2022-11-01 08:18:00', 'title': 'LUMEN WINS $1.5 BILLION DEFENSE INFORMATION SYSTEMS NETWORK CONTRACT', 'text': 'COMPANY WILL PROVIDE ESSENTIAL COMMUNICATIONS SERVICES IN THE ASIA PACIFIC REGION WASHINGTON , NOV. 1, 2022 /PRNEWSWIRE/ --\xa0LUMEN TECHNOLOGIES (NYSE: LUMN) HAS WON A $1.5 BILLION CONTRACT FROM THE DEFENSE INFORMATION SYSTEMS AGENCY (DISA) TO PROVIDE ESSENTIAL NETWORK TRANSPORT AND COMMUNICATIONS SERVICES IN THE U.S. INDO-PACIFIC COMMAND AREA OF RESPONSIBILITY. SPEED READ: LUMEN WILL SUPPLY THE DEFENSE INFORMATION SYSTEMS NETWORK WITH HIGH CAPACITY, END-TO-END COMMUNICATIONS SERVICES THAT ENABLE THE U.S. DEPARTMENT OF DEFENSE TO ACHIEVE U.S. NATIONAL SECURITY OBJECTIVES IN THE 36-NATION ASIA PACIFIC REGION.'}